    "prompt": "# ChoicePayloadDecoder fails to decode Choice ASN.1 types\n\nI found a bug in the ASN.1 decoder when working with Choice types. The decoder fails to properly handle Choice types, causing decoding operations to fail.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nHere's a simple example that demonstrates the issue:\n\n```python\nfrom pyasn1.type import univ, tag\nfrom pyasn1.codec.ber import decoder\n\n# Create a Choice type\nchoice = univ.Choice(\n    componentType=univ.NamedTypes(\n        univ.NamedType('null', univ.Null()),\n        univ.NamedType('boolean', univ.Boolean()),\n        univ.NamedType('octetString', univ.OctetString())\n    )\n)\n\n# Try to decode a simple Null value\nencoded_data = bytes((5, 0))  # Encoded Null value\nresult = decoder.decode(encoded_data, asn1Spec=choice)\n```\n\nThis code fails with an error instead of properly decoding the Choice type.\n\nThe issue also appears when using explicit tags:\n\n```python\n# Create a Choice with explicit tag\ntagged_choice = choice.subtype(explicitTag=tag.Tag(tag.tagClassContext, tag.tagFormatConstructed, 4))\ntagged_choice.setComponentByPosition(0, univ.Null(''))\n\n# Try to decode\nencoded_data = bytes((164, 2, 5, 0))  # Explicitly tagged Null\nresult = decoder.decode(encoded_data, asn1Spec=tagged_choice)\n```\n\nThis also fails to decode properly.\n\nThe problem seems to be related to the inheritance of the ChoicePayloadDecoder class. Can someone look into this?\n\n<END WRITING>\n\nWorkspace and initial working directory (absolute CWD): /testbed",
